# Antigravity & Agent Guardrails

## 1. Specification & Constitution Alignment
- Strict adherence to `.specify/memory/constitution.md` is mandatory for all operations.
- All code modifications must follow the defined Next.js App Router + Tailwind CSS + Shadcn UI stack.
- Never write ad-hoc code without checking specs in `.specify/specs/`.

## 2. Task Routing & Agent Roles (OpenClaw / Antigravity)
- **Heavy Architecture & Planning Phase:** Route structural system design, large refactors, and schema planning to deep reasoning/planning mode before modifying files.
- **Coding & Implementation Phase:** Route focused implementation and code-generation tasks to `gemini-3-flash` via OpenClaw / Antigravity for high-throughput, low-latency execution.
- **Surgical Edits Only:** Prioritize minimal diffs and targeted block edits over full file replacements to avoid token waste and prevent regression.

## 3. Documentation & MCP Integration (Context7 & GitHub)
- **Rule 1 (Context7 First):** Before writing or modifying code involving Next.js App Router, Shadcn UI, Tailwind CSS, or any external library, ALWAYS query the `context7` MCP server (`resolve-library-id` -> `get-library-docs`) to ensure 100% up-to-date syntax and zero hallucination.
- Never guess or hallucinate API parameters or breaking changes in rapidly evolving libraries (such as Next.js, Tailwind v4, or Shadcn UI).
- **Rule 2 (GitHub MCP):** Use the `github` MCP server or `gh` CLI to track feature branches, manage issues, and handle PRs cleanly.

## 4. Code Quality & Pre-Commit Rules
- Format all code with Biome (`npx @biomejs/biome check --write <files>`) prior to saving or committing.
- Respect Husky pre-commit hooks: ensure zero lint errors and proper formatting at all times.

## 5. Git & OpenClaw Workflow Rules
- **Branching Rule:** Never push directly to `main` for new features. Always create a feature branch (`git checkout -b feat/task-name`) based on Spec-Kit tasks in `.specify/specs/`.
- **Pre-Push Check:** Always run `npx @biomejs/biome check --write .` before any `git commit`.
- **OpenClaw Routing:** Use OpenClaw (`gemini-3-flash`) for sub-tasks, web research, and routine component generation.

## 6. Anti-"AI Vibe" & High-Craft Product Design Standards
- **No Generic AI Gradients:** Never use cheap neon rainbow gradients, generic AI mesh blobs, or muddy pastel cards. Use Linear/Vercel-style subtle `1px` borders (`border-white/10`), high-contrast typography, monochrome surfaces with crisp single-color accents, and Bento Grid layouts.
- **Real Data & Micro-Interactions:** Use `@number-flow/react` for metric numbers, `zustand` for complex client states, `nuqs` for URL states, and `drizzle-orm` for real data persistence.

